WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.565
Halley's comet, where it is today.

00:03.265 --> 00:09.822
The most famous comet is out past Neptune now, at the far end of the long, thin loop drawn here.

00:10.272 --> 00:16.059
It last passed the Sun in 1986, and it will be back in 2061.

00:16.509 --> 00:19.917
One thing in this picture is not real: the tail.

00:20.367 --> 00:24.428
Out there Halley is a dark, frozen lump with no tail at all.
